# CS 255 – System Analysis and Design Reflection  

## Client and Project Summary
The client was **DriverPass**, a company that wanted a system to help customers prepare for their driving exams.  
They required a web-based platform that allowed students to:  
- Access study materials and practice tests.  
- Schedule driving lessons with instructors.  
- Track their progress and performance.  

The system needed to be secure, scalable, and user-friendly, ensuring reliable data storage and integration between the online learning resources and lesson scheduling.

---

## Strengths in My Work
I did particularly well in **capturing clear business requirements** and translating them into system requirements. My documentation included both **functional requirements** (like test scheduling and practice exams) and **non-functional requirements** (like system security and scalability). This helped ensure the client’s expectations were fully represented.  

---

## Area I Would Revise
If I could revise one part of my work, I would expand on the **system diagrams**. While I documented requirements thoroughly, I could have created more detailed diagrams showing how data flows between subsystems. This would make it easier for developers and stakeholders to visualize how the system works.  

---

## Interpreting User Needs
The DriverPass users needed a convenient and effective way to prepare for driving exams. I interpreted this by designing a system that combined **educational content** with **lesson scheduling** in a single platform. Considering user needs is critical because a system that doesn’t align with actual user expectations will fail, even if it is technically sound.  

---

## Approach to System Design
I approached system design by first analyzing the **business requirements** and then translating them into technical specifications. I identified constraints, created use case diagrams, and documented both high-level and detailed requirements.  

In the future, I would continue using this structured approach but also incorporate more **iterative design techniques**, such as Agile-based prototyping, to gather feedback earlier and refine designs more quickly.  

---

## Submission Notes
This README serves as my reflection on the **business requirements document** and **system design document** for DriverPass.  
Both documents are included in this repository.  
